WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.710
- So other than like work,

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:03.360
is there anything fun that you're doing

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:07.000
and are looking forward to, I
guess, doing after lockdown?

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.790
- I mean, yeah, I can't wait to, you know,

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:14.280
hang out with friends
and that kind of thing.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.470
And I love...

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:21.470
My wife is one of the most
talented people I've ever met

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:24.020
and watching her perform live,

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.410
or, you know, watching her work,

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.093
she's a dancer and choreographer,

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.060
is just absolutely breathtaking.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:34.140
And so I very much miss that

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.580
and, you know, I also Canadian,

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.770
so I love to go to hockey games. (laughs)

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.200
- [Kelly] Oh my God, that's so Canadian!

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.020
That's awesome. (laughs)

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:47.280
- So those are, you know,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.230
those are, yeah, things I
look forward to and enjoy.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.050
- So wait, you're married to a dancer.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:53.883
I didn't know.

00:00:53.883 --> 00:00:56.455
So, I mean, has this
upped your dance game?

00:00:56.455 --> 00:00:58.223
Do you know some new moves?

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:02.990
- Well, I think what's
so incredible about Emma

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:05.580
is she, like, we've done videos,

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.843
she's included me in her work,
which is incredibly humbling,

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.730
and she's just so incredible

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:16.690
at choreographing for
non-dancers, you know?

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:19.573
So she makes me look like I can dance.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.470
And she also, in the first
season of Umbrella Academy

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:26.160
choreographed this beautiful dance scene.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.910
They're in the park with
all the beautiful lights.

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.490
This very like long dance

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:35.490
and, you know, and Tom hadn't
danced that much before,

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.390
and she's just so fun
and she's such a good,

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.150
she's just so good at
breaking all that down.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:44.490
- Yeah, they make you
look good, man, I know.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.340
I've had to do stuff I'm like, "Nah."

